  "summary": "The restore function must not expose the running state before threads are created. The current implementation sets state.phase to 'running' before ensuring threads exist, which violates the requirement. The fix is to set phase to 'running' only after all threads have been ensured. This change ensures that the state is not marked as running until after threads are created, satisfying the test that checks the phase and thread creation order.",
